  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Complete the accepted M7 advanced research and scope-decision program as an internal evidence-backed milestone only: verify all seven accepted M7 chunks, both work packages and 541 DWF nodes, while preserving research/provider deferrals, three unsent client requests and the distinct owner authorization required for public publication.",
    "value": "A read-only BCL C# checker proves RS122 first-pass, W01/W02 portfolio source SHA identities, the bounded formal/coverage results and exact baseline/target state of eight milestones, seventeen work packages, 58 chunks, 106 requirement IDs, 53 owners, 20 framing sources and six dispositions. Only M7 and the accepted product roadmap become done through DWF. The 1.2.0-candidate remains unpublished; no new advanced/formal public product, external approval, request transmission or future roadmap is claimed.",
    "nextAction": "After durable RS123 success, pause automatic run preparation at the completed accepted roadmap and obtain an explicit owner choice: separately qualify and authorize public package publication, transmit current-revision recipient drafts, or accept a new consumer-driven Math scope. Do not invent M8, adoption or a release.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "Internal M7 completion proves bounded research/decision outcomes, not a publicly released 1.2.0 package or a new advanced mathematics API.",
      "AURA, Decision and MCDM requests remain unsent; recipient revision, owner permission, compatibility tests and rollback are still outstanding.",
      "Precision/interval, tensors, DAG, PlotModel and formal trusted providers remain deferred behind named-consumer, source-free, trusted-base, rights and resource gates.",
      "Any package publication, irreversible licensing, client migration or new roadmap remains subject to a separate explicit owner decision."
    ],
    "achievements": [
      {
        "projectNode": "M7",
        "achievement": "Close the accepted M7 internal advanced-research and scope-decision milestone with source-pinned scientific deferrals, while explicitly withholding public release, external adoption and new roadmap authority."
      }
    ]
  },
